---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy · Luma Pediatrics"
  path="/privacy"
  description="Privacy policy for Luma Pediatrics in McKinney, TX. How we collect, use, and protect information submitted through our website."
>
  <section class="page-hero py-14 md:py-20 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h1 class="mt-5 text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-sm text-[var(--color-muted-foreground)]">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-20 md:pb-28 reveal">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 prose-luma">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy explains how Luma Pediatrics ("we," "us," "our") handles
        information submitted through our website at {SITE.domain}. When clinical services begin,
        protected health information ("PHI") will be handled separately under our Notice of Privacy
        Practices (HIPAA).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Information we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We collect the email address, optional name, consent selection, source page, and submission
        time that you voluntarily provide through the practice-updates form. This signup is not
        patient registration and does not establish a physician-patient relationship.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also collect basic, non-personal log data automatically (IP address, browser type,
        referring URL, pages visited) to operate and improve the site.
      </p>

      <h2>2. How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To send occasional updates about the planned opening and general services.</li>
        <li>To honor unsubscribe, correction, and deletion requests.</li>
        <li>To improve the website's performance, content, and accessibility.</li>
        <li>To comply with applicable law.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. How we share information</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your information. We share information only with service providers that help
        us operate the website and updates list (for example, hosting, analytics, and email or data
        storage providers), and only as necessary to deliver those services. We may disclose information
        when required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies & analytics</h2>
      <p>
        Our website uses Google Analytics to understand site traffic and performance. Analytics may
        collect information such as device type, approximate location, referring page, and pages
        visited. You can limit cookies through your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Children's privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is directed to parents and guardians. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from children under 13 through this website. Clinical care for minors is
        governed by HIPAA and our Notice of Privacy Practices.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect information
        submitted through the website. No system is fully secure; please do not send sensitive
        clinical information through the updates form, email, or text. For current care, contact your
        existing healthcare provider. Secure portal access will be available when scheduling opens.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You may unsubscribe from updates at any time or request access to, correction of, or deletion
        of information submitted through the website by emailing
        {' '}<a href={SITE.contact.emailHref}>{SITE.contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date above will reflect changes.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email <a href={SITE.contact.emailHref}>{SITE.contact.email}</a>
        or write to {SITE.name}, {SITE.address.street}, {SITE.address.city}, {SITE.address.region} {SITE.address.postalCode}.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose-luma h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-foreground);
  }
  .prose-luma p,
  .prose-luma li {
    color: rgba(11, 29, 58, 0.85);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-luma ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  .prose-luma a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
